FRAGMENT: THE KAMIKA LEAVES - translated from a temple margin
Found tucked in the Brahma Vaivarta Purana copy at Puri, written in a different hand. Not part of the canon. Labeled only: Kamika.
I. The Name That Waits

They did not name her at birth. They waited.

On the 11th night of Shravana, in the dark fortnight when the moon is thinning, the priestess went to the river with two bowls. One empty, one full. She said, if the child is to be a desire that fulfills itself, the river will tell us.

The river took the full bowl and left the empty one floating. So they called her Kamika. The one who holds space for true desire to arrive.

